      {
        "id": 206422,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-10-17T18:37:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Folks are forgetting one of WalkingTarget's games:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"WalkingTarget\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/walkingtarget/48/4833_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> WalkingTarget:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Second - Non-Tachyon final damage, CR double skipped except for that he played a single bounty (Kill on Sight) on an automated turret on his last turn and it remained in play until the game ended on Haka's turn that round. No unlock.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This strongly suggests that bounties cannot be played at all on Automated Turrets at least.&nbsp; Perhaps not on any targets other than Ambuscade, perhaps not on devices or villain targets or some other subset.&nbsp; But bounties being triggered/destroyed is irrelevant.</p>\n<p>It still looks like it's: <strong>Ambuscade, Wagner, Chrono, any Tachyon; neither Chrono nor Tachyon can deal the final blow; no bounties can be played on a target other than Ambuscade; Tachyon must not be incapacitated.</strong></p>\n<p>There may be other fail conditions we're not hitting, such as other hero incaps, specific bounties, or specific types of target that bounties can't be played on.&nbsp; Technically we haven't even tested to see if you have to win the game; with Self-Destruct it's possible to lose with no heroes incapped.&nbsp; And maybe Chrono or Tachyon can deal the final blow but not on their turns.&nbsp; At this point I'm kind of inclined to just wait another 4 1/2 hours to see if the devs will throw us a hint in tonight's stream.&nbsp; It wouldn't be helpful if they showed us how to succeed (we know that), but maybe they can show us a way to fail that we haven't encountered/defined yet.</p>",
